        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:40:15.888135+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "d50091f2-1129-44b2-909e-ca921efc3a7b",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 26000,
          "journal_date": "2025-03-23",
          "ocr_text": "S - And fire came out from the burnt offering and the altar, when all the people saw it they shouted and fell in their faces... So fire went out from the Lord and devoured them and they died before the Lord. Lev 10:3\n\nO - After an amazing display of God's power, the priest fell when presumption died. This happened with Peter with he said Jesus was God's son. This happened after Noah's sale family. He should be careful when we stand next to God.\n\nA - Good to walk before God will greater reverence and holiness. A greater honor and respect for who He is.\n\nP - God, help me to walk before you with holiness in integrity and honor. Please forgive me for not honoring you with everything.\n\nQuestions\nWhy did Elisha ask what you have instead of fund raise for her? The husband feared God but lived in debt. He didn't leave his debts in order. She was going to lose her sons on top of losing her husband. She could have been bitter against her husband but honored his memory. She knew he feared God more than the debt he left. She went to her husband mentor Elijah. Why did Elisha ask what he could do? Then ask what she had? He points her to what she has, then sets the stage for him to act in faith. I'm going to multiply what you have but you need to prepare. Why were they instructed to close the door?",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212653198.jpeg",
