          "import_seq": 6003,
          "journal_date": "2025-01-19",
          "ocr_text": "S - Never the less we made our prayer to our god and because of them we set a watch against them day and night. Then Judah said \"The strength of the laborers is failing and there is so much rubbish that we are not able to build the wall.\" And our adversaries said \"They will neither know nor see anything till we come into their midst and kill them and cause their work to cease.\" Neh 4:9-11\n\nO - Nehemiah heard what his people were saying but identified why strength was failing. It wasn't the rubbish. It was the threat of death. Once he solved the problem by arming them and a plan of defense they were able to build again.\n\nA - Correctly identifying why someone won't work is key in leadership. What people say is the problem, many times is not.\n\nP - God, help me to have wisdom to discern the real problems.\n\nS- So I and my brethren servants nor the men of the guard who followed me took off our clothes except that everyone took them off for washing. Neh 4:23\nO- He re established their will to work by equipping them to face their fears of being killed by foes. They were unmotivated and made excuses at first but rubbish, but they were not equipped to fight nor had a plan.\nA- Leaders job is to see the real problem, find the resources, make a plan and give direction to solve the problem then lead by example. His my job to see the real problem, gather resources and make a plan then give clear direction then lead by example.\nP- God help Aali's to be a blessing to our community.",
