        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:42:42.53032+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "e28623df-8196-4a59-841c-a2a182e8fa60",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 39001,
          "journal_date": "2025-05-17",
          "ocr_text": "S- Then Peter said to her, \"How is it that you have agreed together to test the Spirit of the Lord? Look the feet of those who have buried your husband are at the door and they will carry you out\" - so great fear came upon all the church and upon all who heard these things Acts 5:9,11\nO- What was the sin? Lying. When they lied to men, they lied to God. What I do to other believers I do to God. They lied about how much they gave. Seems a harsh punishment. Death is deserving for lying about giving? Doesn't God's grace cover sin? Why death instead of public confession? Why were Sapphiras not killed?\nA- Judgment begins at the house of God. Did they go to heaven? Why would Satan want to fill their heart to lie? About giving?\nP- God help me not to die. Help me to fear you.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212798264.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212798264.jpeg"
          ],
