        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:44:29.087188+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "29e11869-8b53-4000-9b53-01fce9e808f7",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 49000,
          "journal_date": "2025-06-29",
          "ocr_text": "S- Then he also received one talent came and said, \"Lord I knew you to be a hard man, reaping where you have not sown, gathering where you have not sown seed. And I was afraid and went and hid your talent in the ground. Look, there you have what is yours. But the Lord answered to him, \"You wicked and lazy servant, you knew I reaped where I have not sown, and gathered where I have not scattered seed. So you ought to have deposited my money with the bankers and at my coming I would have received my own w/ interest\n\nO- He knew the master's nature of efficiency but did not emulate it. He despised it and became the opposite of his master. The master expected the servant to be like Him. This is the foundation of stewardship.\n\nA- I need to look at God's nature as the measuring stick of righteousness and have this as my aim. 30,60,100x returns- that makes this impossible it's an upward climb an impossible task. So to 100x I wouldn't do it at all\n\nP- God help me to recognize your nature of multiplication and exponential growth. Help me to be more of a faithful steward.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212961727.jpeg",
