          "import_seq": 48003,
          "journal_date": "2025-06-28",
          "ocr_text": "S- For to everyone who has, more will be given out \u0026 he will have abundance; but from him who does not have even what he has will be taken away. Matt 25:29\n\nO- Abundance comes to those who are faithful. Faithfulness involves increasing what we have through trading. Adding value → increase, Muscle, Management, Mouth, Mind. (Time, Talent, Treasure)\n\nA- Spiritual stewardship = Wisdom  Physical stewardship= Faithfulness Prized as Wisdom Reward= Intimacy, Authority Blessed Abundant Blessing to be a blessing ↓ give what — Help Poor\n\nP- God help me to be wise/Faithful/Generous.\n\nS- Then he also received one talent came and said, \"Lord I knew you to be a hard man, reaping where you have not sown, gathering where you have not sown seed. And I was afraid and went and hid your talent in the ground. Look, there you have what is yours. But the Lord answered to him, \"You wicked and lazy servant, you knew I reaped where I have not sown, and gathered where I have not scattered seed. So you ought to have deposited my money with the bankers and at my coming I would have received my own w/ interest\n\nO- He knew the master's nature of efficiency but did not emulate it. He despised it and became the opposite of his master. The master expected the servant to be like Him. This is the foundation of stewardship.\n\nA- I need to look at God's nature as the measuring stick of righteousness and have this as my aim. 30,60,100x returns- that makes this impossible it's an unjust burden so instead I would do 100x I would make a difference\n\nP- God help me to recognize your nature of multiplication and exponential growth. Help me to be more of a faithful steward.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212975634.jpeg",
