          "import_seq": 57003,
          "journal_date": "2025-08-03",
          "ocr_text": "S- For know this, that no fornicator, unclean person nor covetous man, who is an idolater has ANY inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and God. Eph 5:5\n\nO- Paul balances grace with fear of God. There is a consequence for idol worship. It makes us slaves to sin. It makes me disqualified from the inheritance that God has for me.\n\nA- As Jacob took the blessing \u0026 inheritance from Esau, the enemy can steal very inheritance. I give it away when I am overcome with the desires of my flesh. Esau gave it away for a bowl of soup.\n\nP- God forgive me for times I give into my flesh. It is idolatry and a choice to listen to my flesh instead of the Spirit.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213074270.jpeg",
