        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:47:01.474636+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "e9cffa3e-a8f5-434d-8d58-821f17c36f01",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 65002,
          "journal_date": "2025-09-06",
          "ocr_text": "S - Write this: \"Blessed are the dead who die in the Lord from on. Blessed indeed, says the Spirit, that they may rest from their labors, for their deeds follow them.\" Rev 14:13\n\nO - Death is a blessing in the day of tribulation. It is the end of our race. What does it mean that our deeds follow us?\n\nA - I should look as living for Christ as an invitation to die to myself and my flesh till the day that my spirit is united w/ Christ's before it is united with my body in an incorruptible form.\n\nP - Thank you for the glimpse of eternal life and the opportunity to lay my life down for you in the same way you laid your life down for me.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213275234.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213275234.jpeg"
