          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 73003,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-15",
          "ocr_text": "S - He who overcame shall inherit all things And I will be his God and he shall be my son. Rev 21\n\nO - There are only two outcomes Overcoming and being overcome. It's an all or nothing wager. God is a God of extreme. Hot or Cold. Light or Darkness Good or Evil. Heaven or Hell. Satan owns the force.\n\nA - There are worthy opponents in this life to overcome. Doubt. Fear. Lust. Pride. God hasn't called me to mitigate sin but to irradicate it. Through Christ. As I get closer to Him, He will push the darkness out.\n\nP - Jesus draw me close to you. So close that your presence causes me to overcome all enemies of evil and the flesh in my life.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213328654.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213328654.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rev 21",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:48:34.707+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:48:37.994495+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "639ac23a-8834-403a-87ac-4ab63919e048",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 74003,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-19",
          "ocr_text": "S - And behold I am coming quickly and my reward is with me to give to everyone according to his work. Rev 22:12\n\nO - We are not saved BY our works but FOR good works that HE has prepared for us to walk in. We will be judge by how we walked in them.\n\nA - I will not fall into the \"sloppy grace\" mindset but will also not fall into legalism. God saved me for good works that I must be faithful to walk in.\n\nP - God thank you for saving me. Help me to be faithful in all that you have saved me for. Help me not to burn out or to be lazy. Help me to be in love.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213315660.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213315660.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rev 22:12",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:48:37.954+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:48:53.94952+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "eda2fd3a-f4dd-4e81-8a4b-b3e7b4135d30",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 75000,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-20",
          "ocr_text": "S- He who testifies to these things says, 'Surely I am coming quickly'. Amen. Even so, come Lord Jesus.\n\nO- The Lord Himself promises to come quickly and for us to be awake and alert that the day doesn't take us as a thief.\n\nA- I need to watch and pray and stay alert to what is happening in the world to understand the time we are living in.\n\nP- God please help us to live in a way that is surrendered to you everyday. You alone are worthy of my life.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213303688.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213303688.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rev 22:20",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:48:53.902+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:05.369492+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "3570cf22-e19a-442c-9a24-0ec89e7625ad",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 76003,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-27",
          "ocr_text": "S- He whosoever the son of God has life. He who does not have the son of God does not have life. 1 John 5:12\n\nO- The testimony is God has given us eternal life in his Son. All life is found in Christ. I can feel alive in other things. Lust of flesh, lust of eyes, pride of life. I need to choose life. Jesus is life. I cannot eat of both trees. God took the tree of life because 2 trees cannot coexist.\n\nA- I must eat of the tree of life enough to destroy the effects of the other trees in my life.\n\nP- God I'm sorry for choosing the other tree in my life. I need to fall in love w/ you again!",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213368981.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213368981.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "1 John 5:12",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:05.319+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:48:54.175933+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "1602e50e-5f0d-48be-8fb5-fc87f6db4f38",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 75002,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-22",
          "ocr_text": "S- My little children these things I write to you so that you may not sin. And if anyone sins we have an advocate with the Righteous, And He Himself is the propitiation for our sins and not only for ours but also for the whole world. I John 2:1-2\n\nO- John says to confess sins, so that we become free from sin. Not so we can focus on our sin.\n\nA- To be free from sin, I must be honest and transparent about my struggles and sins with others so that I can be free.\n\nP- God I confess my sins to you. Help me to be accountable with trusted brothers.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213303688.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213303688.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "1 John 2:1",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:48:54.134+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:50.025009+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "175c494b-4137-44ba-9b10-68469113ec63",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 80003,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-07",
          "ocr_text": "S- No temptation has overtaken you except such as is common to man, but God is faithful who will not allow you to be tempted beyond what you are able but with the temptation will also make the way of escape that you may be able to bear it.\n\nO- Every temptation I face can be overcome. Every trap of the enemy has an escape of the Lord.\n\nA- I must look for the door. The escape. The exit. Jesus will sit with me and point to the door if I want it.\n\nP- God, help me to give you my time to sit with you so you can reveal to me my escape.\n\nS- Remove your way far from her, and do not go near the door of her house. Prov 5:8\n\nO- The best way to defeat temptation is to get away from it and to live in the light.\n\nA- I need to distance my self from the door of her house. I need to shut the door to strange women.\n\nP- God give me a hatred for sin. A hatred for things that are not of you. Help me to love you more.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213377885.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213377885.jpeg",
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213443720.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "1 Cor 6:13",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:57.982+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:06.481301+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "5d8953f1-191f-46dd-87e8-00f139314b9a",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 82001,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-19",
          "ocr_text": "S- There by the deeds of the law no flesh will be justified in His sight for by the law is the knowledge of sin. Rom 3:20\n\nO- Knowing something is sin has as power to free us from it. It is only in Jesus that I can be set free from the power of sin.\n\nA- I must fix my eyes on Christ and his love and grace for my life.\n\nP- God thank you for the love and grace you have poured out on my life in Jesus.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213431314.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213431314.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rom 3:20",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:06.406+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:05.254961+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "9cd9f9f2-8ab1-41d6-b29a-ece1e8c15aa5",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 76002,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-26",
          "ocr_text": "S- For this is the love of God that we keep his commandments; and his commandments are not burdensome. John 3:13\n\nO- Love is shown in keeping God's commandments because every command has to do with loving God and loving others. Starting w/ any wife.\n\nA- I need to love God first and my wife second. If I struggle to love my wife correctly its because I've lost my love/fear of God. If I fix my relationship w/ God, I'll fix my relationship w/ Jose by default because loving God is loving others.\n\nP- Lord thank you for giving me such an amazing bride. Help me to love her in a way that honors you and is worthy of her.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213368981.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213368981.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "John 3:13",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:05.213+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:49.700861+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "f89a3b92-7754-4b3a-b40a-e13c7ca223f3",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 80000,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-04",
          "ocr_text": "S- He who covers his sins will not prosper. But whoever confesses and forsakes them will have mercy.\n\nO- There is a fear of confession. That it will be met with condemnation. But God calls me to confess. I can leave the results to Him. Then I must forsake my sin by walking in the light. No secrets.\n\nA- I must confess and forsake my sin. Confess to Jose and the pastors. Forsake by being transparent. This is going hurt. Hurt many.\n\nP- God give me courage to confess and forsake. To walk in light.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213377885.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213377885.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Prov 13:13",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:49.653+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:16.288435+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "aa64f21e-1002-4922-99c2-a57eaa9dd44d",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 83001,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-16",
          "ocr_text": "S - It passed over those whose lawless deeds are forgiving and whose sins are covered. Rom 1:7\n\nO - Jesus covers my sins. He is the propitiation for my sin and covers one to the other.\n\nA - The more I know Jesus, the more I fall in love with Him and the more I will hate sin.\n\nP - Jesus, help me to practice your presence and to love you to the point where I hate anything evil everything you call sin.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213418933.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213418933.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rom 1:7",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:16.236+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:25.279786+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "136ac6a0-3ac9-427d-974a-80d973b64641",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 84002,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-22",
          "ocr_text": "S - What shall we say then? Shall we continue in sin that grace may abound? Certainly not. How shall we who died to sin, live any longer in it? Rom 6:1,2\n\nO - Just because forgiven of sin doesn't mean it makes sense to keep doing it. I do it because something in me loves it and I need to learn to hate sin.\n\nA - If I'm dead to sin why do I keep returning to it? How do I invite my heart to fear God's name?\n\nP - God please unite my heart to fear you and to love you with integrity.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213479174.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213479174.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Romans 6:1-2",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:25.065+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:49.817419+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "ad31de06-bffc-4633-8ea1-510ef1a1a179",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 80001,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-05",
          "ocr_text": "S- I have made a covenant w/ my eyes why then shall I look upon a young woman. For what is the allotment from God from above and the inheritance of the almighty from on high.\n\nO- Job played out the long game. He recognized a fleshly desire but saw there was nothing there for him in it. And made a covenant.\n\nA- I need to make a covenant w/ myself. Not to allow my eyes to see worthless things.\n\nP- God help me to set my eyes on things above. Not worthless things of this earth.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213377885.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213377885.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Job 31:1",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:49:49.764+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:16.400098+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "81083c86-964b-4c55-96e0-a3393dd02f4d",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 83002,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-17",
          "ocr_text": "S - New to him who works, the wages are not counted as grace but as debt. But to him who does not work but believes on Him Who justifies the ungodly his faith is accounted for righteousness. Rom 4:4,5\n\nO - If I depend on my own righteousness I will always be paying off a debt that will never be paid. But believing on Jesus, my faith is counted as righteousness\n\nA - I must trust Jesus 100% for my righteousness and let my righteousness and freedom flow from that.\n\nP - God help me to focus on what Jesus did for me and to live in righteousness by faith.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213418933.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213418933.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rom 4:4,5",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:16.353+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:16.172858+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "dcafc0f2-22bb-430f-bf8e-e41ada0d3732",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 83000,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-16",
          "ocr_text": "S - When God set forth as a propitiation by His blood through faith, is demonstrate His righteousness, because in His forbearance, God had passed over the sins that were previously committed. Rom 3:25,26\n\nO - I don't understand the mystery of the propitiation of my sin but Jesus is thee. He covers my sin with His blood and there his presence rests.\n\nA - I must rest in the grace of God. Not to continue in sin but to enjoy His presence.\n\nP - Jesus, help me to be aware of your presence, to live not for righteousness to be righteous but to be with you.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213418933.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213418933.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rom 3:25,26",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:16.118+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:50:25.391163+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "b1e4f1ea-2cea-4eb1-add1-29964eac30ac",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
