          "id": "a22925db-6cd4-4871-bfeb-798befb38bc6",
          "import_batch_id": "0a60c730-b41f-4aa3-af6f-52f2927c7034",
          "import_seq": 4005,
          "journal_date": "2024-01-18",
          "ocr_text": "S- Assuredly, I say to you, wherever this gospel is preached in the whole world, what this woman has done will also be told as a memorial to her.,, Then one of the twelve went to the chief priests and said, \"What are you willing to give me if I deliver Him to you. Matt 26:13-14\n\nO- Teaching on wine \u0026 talents \u0026 sheep vs goats. Wannah \u0026 Judas.\n\nA- I want to be Faithful, generous, Like the woman NOT Judas.\n\nI will do all I can to reach the Lord with all that I have and all that I am. It says \"all\" and I said \"all\" — and that means everything. It means with all my heart, all my soul, all my mind, and all my strength. That's a lot. That means I need to give it everything I have. When I think about what this means, I realize the Lord is asking for my complete devotion and commitment. He wants me to put Him first in everything I do. Not just when it's convenient or when I feel like it, but always. The Lord deserves my best, not my leftovers. I need to be intentional about this. I need to pray more, read my Bible more, and spend more time with Him. I need to let go of the things that are holding me back from fully serving Him. I need to trust Him completely and have faith that He will take care of me. I need to love Him with everything I have.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783218408485.jpg",
