          "ocr_text": "O - John wrote to Gaius commending him for walking in the truth and for his hospitality toward traveling missionaries. He also wrote against Diotrephes who refused to welcome the missionaries and was spreading malicious accusations against John.\nA - We should follow Gaius's example of showing hospitality and kindness to those serving God. We should also be careful not to be like Diotrephes - proud, divisive, and unwilling to submit to godly authority.\nP - Help me to be hospitable and kind to those who are serving you. Give me a heart like Gaius that seeks to help and encourage others in their faith. Protect me from pride and help me to submit to your will.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783218410068.jpg",
