          "date_precision": "year",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "c91b58df-b098-4dff-a576-c2365171058d",
          "import_batch_id": "0a60c730-b41f-4aa3-af6f-52f2927c7034",
          "import_seq": 6001,
          "journal_date": "2024-01-01",
          "ocr_text": "A - And Jesus said, \"Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your mind and with all your strength.\" This is the first and greatest commandment. P - How can I apply this to my life? I need to make sure that God is the center of everything I do. I need to prioritize my relationship with Him above all else. I need to spend time in prayer and Bible study every day. I need to let His Word guide my decisions. I need to be obedient to His commands. I need to trust Him completely. O - The verse emphasizes the totality of our devotion to God. We're not just supposed to love Him a little bit or when it's convenient. We're supposed to love Him with everything we have — our hearts, our souls, our minds, and our strength. O - Jesus said this is the first and greatest commandment. This tells us that loving God should be our highest priority. P - Lord, help me to love You with all my heart, soul, mind, and strength. Help me to make You the center of my life. Help me to be faithful and obedient to You. Amen.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
