          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "a5919b41-9674-484a-84a9-2d8e8f15ac0d",
          "import_batch_id": "0a60c730-b41f-4aa3-af6f-52f2927c7034",
          "import_seq": 8002,
          "journal_date": "2024-01-01",
          "ocr_text": "S \u0026 0\nA prayer of faith brings great blessing to the Lord and He will guide and lead us. The strength that he gives to us will help us to be strong and courageous in all that we do. We must always trust that God has a plan for our lives and He will direct our paths. His promises are sure and He will never fail us. We need to have faith and believe that He can do all things. When we pray with a sincere heart, God will hear and answer our prayers according to His will. He desires for us to grow in our faith and to become more like His son, Jesus Christ. As we walk with Him day by day, He will transform us into the image of Christ. We should spend time in prayer each day and read His word so that we can know Him better. By doing these things, we will experience the joy and peace that comes from having a personal relationship with God.\n\nS- Keep your heart with all diligence for out of it springs the issues of life. Put away from you the froward mouth, and put perverse lips far from you. Let your eyes look straight ahead. Let your eyelids look right before you. Ponder the path of your feet. Let all your ways be established. B not turn to the right or to the left. Remove your foot from evil. Prov 4:23-27\nO- Reigning God from evil is easy once vision is clear. Speak. Control the tongue. Control your vision. Think about your path. Establish it. Don't get distracted. Don't be evil.\nA- Don't talk. Envision. Strategize. Execute. Be consistent. Stay focused. Stop Sinning.\nP- God, help me to pursue your plan for my life.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783218410068.jpg",
