          "import_batch_id": "0a60c730-b41f-4aa3-af6f-52f2927c7034",
          "import_seq": 7003,
          "journal_date": "2024-01-01",
          "ocr_text": "S - MOT: Psalm 5\nO - David is crying out to God in the morning. He is asking God to listen to his prayers \u0026 guide him away from the wicked. He knows that the wicked cannot dwell with God.\nA - I need to cry out to God more often in prayer. I need to trust that He hears me \u0026 will guide me away from sin.\nP - Father, help me to be like David \u0026 cry out to You in prayer. Guide me away from temptation \u0026 help me to stay focused on You.\n\n3 John\n5 Be\nWhoever believes in Jesus and follows Him will have eternal life. The Lord wants all people to come to Him and have a personal relationship with Him. He calls us to tell everyone that Jesus is the way, the truth, and the life. He wants us to share His love with the world and be willing to go to the ends of the earth to do His work. Jesus said, \"All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to me. Therefore go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. And surely I am with you always, to the very end of the age.\" (Matthew 28:18-20) We are called to be witnesses for Jesus, no matter where we are or what circumstances we face. We need to be bold in our faith and willing to stand up for what we believe, even if it means being persecuted. God will give us strength and courage to face any challenge. He promises to never leave us or forsake us. We should always remember that our ultimate purpose is to glorify God and share the gospel with those around us. Every day is an opportunity to make a difference in someone's life by showing them the love of Christ.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783223356710-959830-rot.jpg",
