          "import_seq": 21002,
          "journal_date": "2024-03-27",
          "ocr_text": "S - For as rain comes down and snow at heaven and do not return there but water the earth and make it bring forth and bud, that it may give seed to the sower and bread to the eater. So shall my word be that goes forth from my mouth. It shall not return to me void but it shall accomplish what I please and it shall prosper in the thing for which I sent it. Isaiah 55:10-11\n\nO - God's word is like rain. It gives seed to sew. It gives bread to eat. It will accomplish His will. It will prosper what God wants to prosper.\n\nA - I need to read Your word more. I need to let that rain water my life. It's your word that brings success to my life. Not other things.\n\nP - God please help me to be faithful to your word. Help me to abide in a place where rain falls. Help me clear distractions from my life.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
