          "import_seq": 44003,
          "journal_date": "2024-06-26",
          "ocr_text": "S- But if we hope for what we do not see, we eagerly wait for it with perseverance. Who can separate us from the love of Christ? Shall tribulation, or distress or persecution or famine, or nakedness or peril or sword? As it is written, For your sake we are killed all day long. We are accounted as sheep for the slaughter.\nO- NT Christians were persecuted, but held on to faith. The love of Christ compelled them.\nA- I want this love to compel me into suffering. I want to be purified.\nP- God help me to embrace what you have for me and the church.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783218420135.jpg",
