          "import_seq": 37003,
          "journal_date": "2024-05-30",
          "ocr_text": "S- I am dark but lovely O daughters of Jerusalem. Like the tents of Kedar, Like the curtains of Salma. Do not look upon me because I am dark. Because the sun has gazed upon me. My mother's sons were angry with me. They made me the keeper of the vineyards but my own vineyard I have not kept. SOS 1:5,6\n\nO- Those who were supposed to love her didn't and put her to hard labor. She could have been in the kings palace but instead is in the hot sun because she chose to love her be loved.\n\nA- There is a price to pay for love. Patience in waiting. Saving and consecrating oneself for another. Denying the advances and opportunity. Being attracted to someone for who they are, not what they have. Others will not understand. Others will despise. Love will cost her K. She became dark.\n\nP- God help me to understand love.",
