        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T02:37:50.865865+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "b2b03b86-3151-48ef-bac8-df5a9e2cc068",
          "import_batch_id": "0a60c730-b41f-4aa3-af6f-52f2927c7034",
          "import_seq": 38002,
          "journal_date": "2024-06-02",
          "ocr_text": "S- I have compared you, my love, to my filly among Pharaoh's chariots. Your cheeks are lovely with ornaments, your neck with chains of gold. SOS 1:9\nO- The king is speaking and compare her to the chariots of horses from egypt. he was not supposed to have. I e shadowed behind her was revealing he loves his willingness to live a life of reproach. And that he was willing to take his father's cohabiting? It was not right he had those horses. It's not pure love to compare her to those horses. He also talks of her neck with gold and wants her heart. To add to his collection of riches.\nA- The world has a spirit that is seductive. It's the wisdom of the world. It multiplies gold, chariots from Egypt, Women - It's a blessing from God but can corrupt our hearts. The king wanted the Bride. But didn't love the Bride. The shepherd loved the bride. The daughter's of Jerusalem was mesmerized by the king and loved the Bride and wanted her to be happy and wanted her to be with the king. The fear of lack could draw her to the king. Good shepherd tells her, look at the lilies of the field. Luke 12:27\nP- God help me not to be seduced by fear of lack or by the attractiveness of riches. help me to trust in you and to sow into your kingdom.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783218418567.jpg",
          "photo_urls": [
