          "ocr_text": "Anchor\nWaves of sorrow\n\n2. Plant your hope on eternity. - Waves of sorrow pass. Even in tragedy?\n\n3. Pain has power - You can comfort others. Don't isolate. You can be powerful in pain.\n\n4. Great Purpose - Solomon was born. The death of Solomon's son was not the end of the purpose of David's life.\n\nIn the midst of pain \u0026 tragedy, God's purpose promise. Presence remains. Remain as our strength and foundation that will last far beyond the feeling of sorrow and pain.\n\n1. Don't let the enemy push you away from God.\n   • Anger w/ God\n   • Doubt his love\n   • Regret, guilt, condemnation\n   • You Be confident that God loves you and wants to hold your hand \u0026 carry you through this.\n\n2. Anchor yourself in the hope of eternity.\n   • Waves of sorrow \u0026 despair wash over you, anchor your thoughts on the reunion with Kiah.\n   • Meditate on the shortness of this life and the vastness of eternity.\n   • This world is all we have experienced but this world is not our home.\n\n3. Comfort others in your pain. You become powerful when you are in pain.\n   • Katherine McCleed.\n   • Jesus",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
