          "import_seq": 5000,
          "journal_date": "2024-01-01",
          "ocr_text": "Ecclesiastes 3 Meditation\n\nIn 1 month I've learned that Ecclesiastes is a guide. A legacy left by the wisest man to help us bear the troubles \u0026 sorrows of life to hope to have the hope that all is not lost. A promise that under God's dominion all things work together for His good \u0026 our benefit.\n\nObservation:\n- To everything a season: every purpose has its time \u0026 place\n- There is a time to be silent \u0026 a time to speak\n- God has made everything beautiful in its time\n- God has set eternity in the hearts of men\n- a man cannot fathom what God has done from beginning to end\n\nApplication:\nKnowing that every season of life has a purpose. \u0026 that God has set everything in its time should free me from the anxiety of the unknown. I have the promise that my life, my pain, my sorrows are not in vain. They are all part of His perfect plan.\n\nPrayer:\nGod help me to trust in Your timing. Help me to embrace both the seasons of joy \u0026 the seasons of sorrow. Knowing that You are the author of all seasons \u0026 that You have made everything beautiful in its time. Help me to find peace in this truth.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783218409790.jpg",
