          "ocr_text": "O- Nehemiah had supplies from the king and favor of God to rebuild. But he didn't make a big deal about it and told no one why.\n\nA- There is a right time for public disclosure. It was after gathering resources for the project.\n\nP- God help me to have wisdom and call forward in this project.\n\nS- Then I said to them, you see the distress that we are in, how Jerusalem lies in waste, and its gates are burned with fire. Come and let us build the wall of Jerusalem that we may no longer be a reproach. And then I told them of the hand of my God which had been good upon me and also of the king's words that he had spoken to me. So they said, \"Let us arise and build.\" Neh 2:17,16\n\nO- He starts with their pain. Then the cause of their pain. Then the action to remove the pain. He anticipates their rebuttal but talked to the king already and shared that after, A- Start with the problem. Share the solution. Clear objections to the solution.\n\nP- God give me wisdom to serve the next generation of Maui.",
